Package: appauth
Title: Secure Authentication and User Management for 'shiny' Applications
Version: 0.12.0
Authors@R:
    c(person("Alexey", "Seleznev", , "selesnow@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0410-7385")),
      person("Netpeak", role = "cph"))
Description: Provides login, user management and access control for 'shiny'
    applications backed by 'SQLite' (the default), 'DuckDB', 'MySQL' / 'MariaDB'
    or 'PostgreSQL'. Features include password login with hashed-only storage,
    cookie-based auto-login, brute-force protection, blocking and deleting users
    while keeping the last administrator, password recovery by email with
    one-time links, two-factor authentication with time-based one-time
    passwords, sign-in with 'Google' ('OpenID' Connect) with optional disabling
    of password login, opt-in self-registration with email confirmation and
    automatic account creation for verified 'Google' users, server-side
    permission checks, ready-made user interface modules with extension points,
    and versioned database schema migrations.
